mode: "100644"
text: "# Cover letter: Jordan Reyes, Software Engineer, Google Cloud Infrastructure\n\nHi Maya,\n\nYour post about how your team runs design reviews is the reason I am writing. I ran design reviews the same way for the payments API rebuild at Brightline Labs, and I would like to bring that habit to the Software Engineer role on the Google Cloud Infrastructure team.\n\nFor 3 years at Brightline Labs I have built backend services in Go. I rebuilt the payments API, cutting p99 latency 38% across 4M requests a day. I shipped the ML ranking service behind our search, which lifted click-through 12%. I also lead on-call for 9 services, and the automated runbooks I wrote cut pages 60%. That is the part of the job I like most: a service that stays fast and quiet after launch.\n\nGoogle Cloud is where that work matters most. Customers build their own products on this infrastructure, so latency and reliability are the product itself. I want to work on those problems with a team that reviews designs carefully and owns what it ships, and your team's posts suggest it does both.\n\nWould you be open to a short call in the next few weeks about what the team is building next? I would value your view on where someone with my background could help first.\n\nThank you for reading,\nJordan Reyes\n"
